This is an UNOFFICIAL fix for the problem causing 'H's and/or 'f's placed
on the screen by PC Nethack 3.0e.

The termcap.cnf file needs to be changed.

Before changing anything, make sure that you backup the file to be changed,
and save it in a safe place, since the next set of patches is made to work
with the original distribution + official patches.  This is UNOFFICIAL.

In the TERMCAP.CNF file (or TERMCAP, depending on what you have called it),
there is a line like the following in the ansi-color and other sections:
cm:\E[%i%d;%dH
It should be changed to:
cm:\E[%i%2;%2H
ANSI.SYS and also NNANSI.SYS(I think) expect row and column numbers to be
2 numeric characters long.  i.e., \E[09;09H moves the cursor to row 9, column
9, and \E[9;9H moves the cursor, and prints the H.  I'm not sure why.
Changing the %d in the cm part to %2 tells termlib.lib(Fred Fish's) that
the terminal needs two character long numbers, and fixes the problem quite
nicely. 

